      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Replace the numbered function-by-function diff narration with a concise prose paragraph summarizing *why* unchecked `raw_read16()` calls were problematic and *what* changed conceptually (or split into focused commits per function as noted in the review summary):\n\n**Option A (if kept as a single CL):**\n```text\nisl923x: Check raw_read16 errors in RAA489000 charger handlers\n\nSeveral RAA489000 charger callbacks in driver/charger/isl923x.c did not\ncheck the return status of raw_read16() before using the read value,\ncausing I2C read failures to report current calculated from an\nuninitialized stack variable or write uninitialized/stale values back to\nprimary charger control registers.\n\nCheck raw_read16() errors in raa489000_get_actual_current() and\nraa489000_enable_linear_charge(), and use raw_update16() in\nraa489000_set_vsys_compensation() so failed reads abort before modifying\nor writing back register state.\n\nBUG\u003db:573999103\nTEST\u003d./twister -T zephyr/test/drivers -s drivers.isl923x -s drivers.raa489000\n\nChange-Id: Iacf5a3dffacdc03bb82e3f9a0296fb6103bb6c6b\n```\n\n**Option B (if split into independent CLs per function):**\n- **CL 1:**\n```text\nisl923x: Check raw_read16 error in raa489000_get_actual_current\n\nraa489000_get_actual_current() did not check the return status of\nraw_read16() before scaling the register value, causing I2C read\nfailures to populate the output current from an uninitialized stack\nvariable. Return early on read error to match isl923x_get_current() and\nraa489000_get_actual_voltage().\n\nBUG\u003db:573999103\nTEST\u003d./twister -T zephyr/test/drivers -s drivers.isl923x -s drivers.raa489000\n```\n- **CL 2:**\n```text\nisl923x: Check raw_read16 error in raa489000_enable_linear_charge\n\nraa489000_enable_linear_charge() wrote ISL923X_REG_CONTROL2 back to the\nprimary charger even when reading its current value failed, corrupting\nthe register with an uninitialized stack variable. Only modify and write\nISL923X_REG_CONTROL2 when raw_read16() succeeds.\n\nBUG\u003db:573999103\nTEST\u003d./twister -T zephyr/test/drivers -s drivers.isl923x -s drivers.raa489000\n```\n- **CL 3:**\n```text\nisl923x: Avoid writing CONTROL10 on read error in set_vsys_compensation\n\nraa489000_set_vsys_compensation() unconditionally wrote\nRAA489000_REG_CONTROL10 on the primary charger even when reading its\ncurrent value failed, overwriting it with the secondary charger register\nvalue. Use raw_update16() so the register is only written when the read\nsucceeds.\n\nBUG\u003db:573999103\nTEST\u003d./twister -T zephyr/test/drivers -s drivers.isl923x -s drivers.raa489000\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/345dc698-67d3-4c2c-9623-427f20348fd3)",
