      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested — Please address inline comments.**\n\n### Review Summary\n\n* **Functionality**: The three changes in `driver/charger/isl923x.c` properly prevent propagating or writing back uninitialized/stale I2C register values when `raw_read16()` fails in `raa489000_get_actual_current()`, `raa489000_enable_linear_charge()`, and `raa489000_set_vsys_compensation()`.\n* **Architecture \u0026 Component Fit**: The error handling changes and emulator-based unit tests fit cleanly within the existing `isl923x`/`raa489000` charger driver and Zephyr `i2c_common_emul` test framework.\n* **Code Simplicity**: In `raa489000_set_vsys_compensation()` (`driver/charger/isl923x.c`, lines 1621–1626), the manual `raw_read16()` / `if (!rv)` / bitwise-OR / `raw_write16()` sequence duplicates the existing `raw_update16()` helper and should be replaced with `rv \u003d raw_update16(CHARGER_PRIMARY, RAA489000_REG_CONTROL10, RAA489000_C10_ENABLE_DVC_CHARGE_MODE, MASK_SET);`, matching `raa489000_enable_linear_charge()`.\n* **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability**: Aside from simplifying the read-modify-write in `raa489000_set_vsys_compensation()`, the C code follows the surrounding driver conventions cleanly.\n* **Security**: No security vulnerabilities or unsafe memory accesses were identified; checking `raw_read16()` return values prevents acting on uninitialized stack data (`int reg` in `raa489000_enable_linear_charge()`).\n* **Testing**: In `zephyr/test/drivers/raa489000/src/raa489000.c` (`test_charger_read_errors`, lines 144–189):\n  * Both `raa489000_enable_linear_charge()` and `raa489000_set_vsys_compensation()` already returned `EC_ERROR_UNKNOWN` when `raw_read16()` failed prior to this CL (because `rv` was non-zero from `raw_read16()` and `i2c_common_emul_set_read_fail_reg()` only fails reads, so the subsequent `raw_write16()` succeeded and `rv |\u003d 0` remained non-zero). To verify the actual fix—that a failed read does not trigger a write that corrupts `ISL923X_REG_CONTROL2` or `RAA489000_REG_CONTROL10`—the test should inspect the emulator registers via `isl923x_emul_peek_reg()`.\n  * Assertions should verify exact return codes (`zassert_equal(EC_ERROR_INVAL, ...)` instead of `zassert_not_equal(EC_SUCCESS, ...)`) and verify `zassert_equal(0, current)` when `get_actual_current` succeeds.\n* **CL Size \u0026 Scope**: `gerrit info` reports `Size: M (+91, -9)` (~17 production lines modified in `driver/charger/isl923x.c` and ~83 lines in test/devicetree/config files). While the total line count is small, the CL bundles three independently revertible bug fixes across three distinct `isl923x_drv` API methods (`get_actual_current`, `enable_linear_charge`, and `set_vsys_compensation`), enumerated as a 3-item list in the commit message. Consider splitting this into three focused CLs so each fix can be reviewed and reverted independently:\n  1. **CL 1**: `isl923x: Check raw_read16 return value in raa489000_get_actual_current` (`driver/charger/isl923x.c` lines 536–542 and the `get_actual_current` test case in `zephyr/test/drivers/raa489000/src/raa489000.c`).\n  2. **CL 2**: `isl923x: Use raw_update16 in raa489000_enable_linear_charge` (`driver/charger/isl923x.c` lines 971–993, `zephyr/test/drivers/raa489000/prj.conf`, and the `enable_linear_charge` test case in `zephyr/test/drivers/raa489000/src/raa489000.c`).\n  3. **CL 3**: `isl923x: Avoid writing RAA489000_REG_CONTROL10 on read failure in raa489000_set_vsys_compensation` (`driver/charger/isl923x.c` lines 1621–1626, `zephyr/test/drivers/raa489000/raa489000.dts`, and the `set_vsys_compensation` test case in `zephyr/test/drivers/raa489000/src/raa489000.c`).\n* **Commit Message**: The commit message body uses a 3-item numbered list that narrates the diff function-by-function using raw C expressions; see the inline comment on `/COMMIT_MSG` for a concise prose replacement.\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/345dc698-67d3-4c2c-9623-427f20348fd3)",
