      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Strengthen `test_charger_read_errors` so that it verifies registers are not overwritten on read failure and asserts exact expected outputs on both error and success paths:\n\n1. **Verify no register write occurs on read failure in `enable_linear_charge` and `set_vsys_compensation`:** Even without the fixes in `driver/charger/isl923x.c`, a failed `raw_read16()` already set `rv` to `EC_ERROR_INVAL` while the subsequent `raw_write16()` succeeded, causing both functions to return `EC_ERROR_UNKNOWN`. As written, `zassert_equal(EC_ERROR_UNKNOWN, ...)` passes even if the fixes in `raa489000_enable_linear_charge()` and `raa489000_set_vsys_compensation()` are reverted. Reset `primary_emul` registers before testing and assert via `isl923x_emul_peek_reg()` that `ISL923X_REG_CONTROL2` and `RAA489000_REG_CONTROL10` remain `0` when the respective read fails, and are updated as expected when the read succeeds.\n2. **Assert exact error code and output values:**\n   - Replace `zassert_not_equal(EC_SUCCESS, ...)` on line 164 with `zassert_equal(EC_ERROR_INVAL, ...)` to match the exact error returned by `i2c_common_emul_set_read_fail_reg()`.\n   - After `zassert_ok(isl923x_drv.get_actual_current(CHARGER_PRIMARY, \u0026current))` on line 184, assert the resulting value of `current` (`zassert_equal(0, current)`).\n   - Use distinct values for `.rsys_mo` / `.rbatt_mo` and `current_ma` / `voltage_mv` in `set_vsys_compensation()` calls rather than identical `50, 50` and `0, 0` pairs.\n\n```c\nZTEST(tcpc_raa489000, test_charger_read_errors)\n{\n\tconst struct emul *primary_emul \u003d\n\t\tEMUL_DT_GET(DT_NODELABEL(isl923x_emul));\n\tconst struct emul *sec_emul \u003d\n\t\tEMUL_DT_GET(DT_NODELABEL(isl923x_sec_emul));\n\tstruct i2c_common_emul_data *primary_common \u003d\n\t\temul_isl923x_get_i2c_common_data(primary_emul);\n\tstruct ocpc_data ocpc \u003d {\n\t\t.rsys_mo \u003d 52,\n\t\t.rbatt_mo \u003d 40,\n\t};\n\tint current \u003d -1;\n\n\tisl923x_emul_reset_registers(primary_emul);\n\tisl923x_emul_reset_registers(sec_emul);\n\tcharge_set_active_chg_chip(CHARGER_SECONDARY);\n\n\t/* Fail reading RAA489000_REG_ADC_CHARGE_CURRENT in get_actual_current */\n\ti2c_common_emul_set_read_fail_reg(primary_common,\n\t\t\t\t\t  RAA489000_REG_ADC_CHARGE_CURRENT);\n\tzassert_equal(EC_ERROR_INVAL,\n\t\t      isl923x_drv.get_actual_current(CHARGER_PRIMARY,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t     \u0026current));\n\tzassert_equal(current, -1);\n\n\t/* Fail reading ISL923X_REG_CONTROL2 in enable_linear_charge */\n\ti2c_common_emul_set_read_fail_reg(primary_common, ISL923X_REG_CONTROL2);\n\tzassert_equal(EC_ERROR_UNKNOWN,\n\t\t      isl923x_drv.enable_linear_charge(CHARGER_PRIMARY, true));\n\tzassert_equal(0, isl923x_emul_peek_reg(primary_emul,\n\t\t\t\t\t       ISL923X_REG_CONTROL2));\n\n\t/* Fail reading primary RAA489000_REG_CONTROL10 in set_vsys_compensation */\n\tisl923x_emul_reset_registers(primary_emul);\n\tisl923x_emul_set_device_id(sec_emul, RAA489000_DEV_ID_B0);\n\ti2c_common_emul_set_read_fail_reg(primary_common,\n\t\t\t\t\t  RAA489000_REG_CONTROL10);\n\tzassert_equal(EC_ERROR_UNKNOWN,\n\t\t      isl923x_drv.set_vsys_compensation(CHARGER_SECONDARY,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\u0026ocpc, 1000, 4200));\n\tzassert_equal(0, isl923x_emul_peek_reg(primary_emul,\n\t\t\t\t\t       RAA489000_REG_CONTROL10));\n\n\ti2c_common_emul_set_read_fail_reg(primary_common,\n\t\t\t\t\t  I2C_COMMON_EMUL_NO_FAIL_REG);\n\tzassert_ok(isl923x_drv.get_actual_current(CHARGER_PRIMARY, \u0026current));\n\tzassert_equal(0, current);\n\tzassert_ok(isl923x_drv.enable_linear_charge(CHARGER_PRIMARY, true));\n\tzassert_not_equal(0, isl923x_emul_peek_reg(primary_emul,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t   ISL923X_REG_CONTROL2) \u0026\n\t\t\t\t     GENMASK(15, 13));\n\tzassert_equal(EC_ERROR_UNIMPLEMENTED,\n\t\t      isl923x_drv.set_vsys_compensation(CHARGER_SECONDARY,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\u0026ocpc, 1000, 4200));\n\tzassert_not_equal(0, isl923x_emul_peek_reg(primary_emul,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t   RAA489000_REG_CONTROL10) \u002